<title>FRANCE: Loreal 1997 H1 sales breakdown.</title>
<headline>Loreal 1997 H1 sales breakdown.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>     Turnover				 34.02 vs 30.11</p>
<p>	- includes Q2			 17.51 vs 15.29</p>
<p>	   - cosmetics			14.36 vs 12.56</p>
<p>	   - Synthelabo (drugs)	    2.90 vs  2.50</p>
<p>	   - dermatology		     0.17 vs  0.13</p>
<p>	   - other			     0.09 vs  0.11</p>
<p>	- Q1				    16.51 vs 14.82</p>
<p>	   - cosmetics			13.36 vs 11.96</p>
<p>	   - Synthelabo (drugs)	    2.85 vs  2.62</p>
<p>	   - dermatology		     0.18 vs  0.12</p>
<p>	   - other			     0.12 vs  0.13</p>
<p>NOTE - L'Oreal said in the BALO official bulletin that consolidated half-year sales rose 13 percent. On a comparable structure and at level exchange rates, the rise was 8.1 percent.</p>
<p>Its cosmetics sales rose 13.1 percent, or 8.1 percent on a like for like first half of 1996.</p>
<p>L'Oreal has a 56 percent stake in pharmaceuticals firm Synthelabo.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
